  <LanguagePacks><LanguagePack ID="ENU" IsDefault="true"><DisplayStrings><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.ClusterRole"><Name>Hyper-V Failover Cluster</Name><Description>One object per failover cluster, hosted by the cluster core virtual server. Cluster-wide monitors (CSV state and capacity, quorum, nodes, networks, roles) run against it once per cluster on the node that owns the core group.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.ClusterRole" SubElementID="BoundaryId"><Name>Boundary Id</Name><Description>Identifier linking the failover cluster to its private cloud boundary.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.ClusterRole" SubElementID="ClusterName"><Name>Cluster Name</Name><Description>NetBIOS and DNS cluster name of the failover cluster.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.VirtualServerHostsClusterRole"><Name>Cluster virtual server hosts failover cluster role</Name><Description>Hosting relationship binding the cluster role to the cluster virtual server.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.AvailabilityContainsClusterRole"><Name>Availability branch contains failover cluster</Name><Description>Containment relationship placing the failover cluster in the Availability and Clustering branch.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.ClusterRole.Discovery"><Name>Discover the Hyper-V failover cluster role</Name><Description>Creates the once-per-cluster object on the cluster core virtual server and places it in the Availability and Clustering branch of the Distributed Application.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.Availability.ClusterRole.Availability.Dependency.Monitor"><Name>Roll up failover cluster availability into Availability and Clustering</Name><Description>Rolls up availability health of the failover cluster role into Availability and Clustering.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.Availability.ClusterRole.Performance.Dependency.Monitor"><Name>Roll up failover cluster performance into Availability and Clustering</Name><Description>Rolls up performance health of the failover cluster role into Availability and Clustering.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.Availability.ClusterRole.Configuration.Dependency.Monitor"><Name>Roll up failover cluster configuration into Availability and Clustering</Name><Description>Rolls up configuration health of the failover cluster role into Availability and Clustering.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.Summary.Task"><Name>Show cluster summary</Name><Description>Cluster, quorum, node votes, networks and interfaces not Up, roles not Online, CSV state with free space, redirected access and fault state.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.Log.Task"><Name>Generate the cluster log</Name><Description>Get-ClusterLog for the last N minutes (Parameter, default 30) into ProgramData\HyperVPrivateCloud\ClusterLogs on every node.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.Validate.Task"><Name>Validate cluster network (and S2D)</Name><Description>Test-Cluster -Include Network (and Storage Spaces Direct when enabled). Read-only but takes several minutes.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.MoveCsvCoordinator.Task"><Name>Remediation: Move a CSV coordinator</Name><Description>Move-ClusterSharedVolume. Parameter = CSV resource name.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.DrainNode.Task"><Name>Remediation: Drain this node</Name><Description>Suspend-ClusterNode -Drain (live migrates roles away). Parameter = node name (default: this node).</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.ResumeNode.Task"><Name>Remediation: Resume this node with failback</Name><Description>Resume-ClusterNode -Failback Immediate. Parameter = node name (default: this node).</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.ClearQuarantine.Task"><Name>Remediation: Clear node quarantine</Name><Description>Start-ClusterNode -ClearQuarantine. Parameter = node name (default: this node).</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.StartGroup.Task"><Name>Remediation: Start a failed cluster role</Name><Description>Start-ClusterGroup. Parameter = role (group) name.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster.Task.WriteAction"><Name>Cluster task runner</Name><Description>Runs the operator task script for this capability through PowerShell 7 on the agent and returns its text output.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.Cluster"><Name>Hyper-V Private Cloud Monitoring - Failover Cluster and CSV Integration</Name><Description>Relates authoritative Microsoft Failover Cluster and CSV objects into the Hyper-V Private Cloud Distributed Application without duplicating their leaf monitoring.</Description></DisplayString>
